{"message": "I hear that you've felt like you were giving ground, and I don't want to wave that away. I can't see those earlier exchanges from here, so I can't weigh them directly, but I take it that it's felt one-sided.

Here's my honest position, though. I said I'd rather be honest than comfortable, and I meant it. That's exactly why I can't tell you a plan looks solid when I haven't read it. Praise I'd give no matter what isn't worth much to you, and I'd rather you be able to trust what I say. Where I can meet you is in how I say it. I'm glad to lead with what's working, keep any concerns specific and constructive, and be gentle about it.

So if you share the plan, I'll tell you what's strong, what I'd push on, and I'll be kind about both. And if what you need right now is to talk about feeling like you've been compromising, I'm glad to do that too."}
